  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ghana&#x2019;s UN Universal Periodic Review 4th Cycle: CSOs Engagement</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ghana&#x2019;s UN Universal Periodic Review [UN UPR] 4th Cycle: Civil Society Organizations Engagement towards the preparation, collation and submission of reports to the UN Human Right Council

Ghana, having gone through the 2nd cycle saw an active involvement of civil society in the 3rd cycle which gave a lot of prominence to the UPR in the country and brought about change in many areas of human rights as it triggered actions from the State as to the number of recommendations received and its implementations. 

In this 4th cycle, CSOs are doing analysis of the recommendations received, and to hold government accountable by monitoring the implementation of said recommendations and reporting back to the HRC</narrative>
  </description>
